Record phase, hour, enemy, AI states.
But note `_beginJumpscare` sets phase jumpscare, and update returns; we stop immediately. Then record. Death time = elapsed.
For a perfect player policy, we need to call game methods between updates. We can implement in page.evaluate:
```
function policy() {
  const m = g.ai.muzan;
  if (m && m.active && m.state==='manifest') {
    if (g.monitor) g.setMonitor(false);
    if (!g.flashlight) g.toggleFlashlight(true);
    g.lookYaw = 0; g.lookPitch = 0; // aim at Muzan
    return;
  }
  // vent
  const n = g.ai.nezuko;
  if (n && n.active && n.state==='ventDoor') {
    if (g.monitor) { g.setCamera('vent'); }
    else { g.setMonitor(true); g.setCamera('vent'); }
    // keep flashlight off while monitor
    return;
  }
  // doors
  const leftAlert = g.doorAlerts.left; right...
  if (leftAlert || rightAlert) {
    if (g.monitor) g.setMonitor(false);
    if (leftAlert && !g.doors.left) g.toggleDoor('left');
    if (!leftAlert && g.doors.left) g.toggleDoor('left');
    ...
    return;
  }
  // otherwise open doors, lower monitor, flashlight off
  if (g.doors.left) g.toggleDoor('left');
  if (g.doors.right) g.toggleDoor('right');
  if (g.monitor) g.setMonitor(false);
  if (g.flashlight) g.toggleFlashlight(false);
  // occasionally check cameras? 
}
```
But `g.doorAlerts` is updated in `_placeCharacters` each update. Good.
However, when we call `setMonitor(false)` and `toggleDoor`, these methods call `_pushState` which invokes callbacks and DOM; fine. They also require phase playing.

For vent, if we open monitor and set camera vent, `_updateAI` sees activeCam==='vent' and ventSeen increments; after .72s retreat. Good. But while monitor open, door alerts may occur; the policy will handle on next step by lowering monitor and closing. Fine.

For Muzan, `g.lookYaw=0` and flashlight; `_isAimingAtMuzan` dot ~0.999. Good. But `g.toggleFlashlight(true)` requires battery >0 and monitor false. If battery is low, it fails. We can manage battery: only use for Muzan. In the policy, if manifest, turn on. If battery 0, can't. The battery recovers when off. Muzan manifests every ~30s; 1.18s each, so fine.

Need to avoid calling `toggleDoor` when monitor open; we lower first. But `setMonitor(false)` returns if powerOut/redAlert; if redAlert (Muzan manifest), we handle Muzan first. Good.

For doors: if a character is at the door and we close, they retreat after .48s; then `doorAlerts` false; policy opens the door next step. But opening immediately may allow another character at the same door to attack? The character is in retreat; no. Fine. Power drain is minimal.

But there is a subtlety: closing the door triggers `_retreat` after .48s, but the policy opens it as soon as `doorAlerts` false, which is after `_placeCharacters` updates. Good.

To survive the whole night, the policy must also handle power: with both doors closed only during alerts, power should last. Monitor open only for vent. Base drain .1/s * 210s = 21 power. Door usage .29/s for ~0.5s per alert. Monitor .19/s for .72s per vent. So power remains high. Good.

But Giyu only moves while monitor open; if we never watch cameras, he never attacks. The policy only opens monitor for vent; if Giyu active, he may move then. But we open monitor for .72s; Giyu's moveTimer decreases by dt*1 while monitor open, so he may move a few times across the night. He could reach the door and attack. Policy handles door alert. Fine.

Tanjiro freezes while watched on camera; not relevant.

Inosuke: if watched on camera, speed 1.7 (moves faster). Our monitor only for vent, not his room. Fine.

